.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "set_context" "set_context"
.SH NAME
set_context \- Inject an external cell context into the model as the control baseline of the following
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIset_context(\fBgps\fR as <generic> GPSModel, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBlogcpm\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Inject an external cell context into the model as the control baseline of the following
 in silico perturbation experiments.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgps\fB \fR\- the trained model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- 
 a character vector of the gene id of the context profile; the ids must live in the same
 identifier space as the model (Ensembl gene id for the human model).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlogcpm\fB \fR\- 
 a numeric vector of the `log2(CPM + 1)` expression value of the context, in the same
 order as **genes**. The caller is responsible for the library size
 normalization and for the log transform; the model only applies its own z-score.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
TRUE when the context has been applied; an R# error message object is returned when the
 gene ids do not overlap the modelled genes at all.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Genes of the model that are missing from **genes** keep their own mean
 (that is a z-score of zero), so a context is allowed to cover only the genes of the
 sequencing panel.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GPS
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
